Camille,<br />
<br />
I have now reached or accounted for everyone named in the 2011 summary reco=
rd. There is no institutional memory left on either side.<br />
<br />
Rosalind Achterberg, branch chief, retired in 2019. She remembers the firm =
and remembers "a custody question" but will not put anything more specific =
than that in a declaration and I would not want her to.<br />
<br />
Desmond Whitlatch, examiner in charge, left the Commission in 2015 and has =
been at FINRA since. He was more definite - he says there was a deficiency =
letter and that the firm gave the staff an undertaking of some kind, but he=
 has no documents, and his recollection thirteen years on is not something =
we want to be resting on by itself.<br />
<br />
Tirado Hobbs LLP, the firm's counsel of record in 2011, dissolved in 2018. =
Its client files went to storage under a vendor that has since been acquire=
d, and Respondent's present counsel tells me nothing from the 2011 engageme=
nt came across.<br />
<br />
Nathaniel Okuma, assistant regional director, retired in 2021 and did not r=
espond to two messages. Priya Raghunathan left the Commission in 2017 and i=
s now in private practice; she recalls drafting a findings memorandum but n=
ot its contents.<br />
<br />
On the firm's side, the chief compliance officer of the period, Marguerite =
Vasseur-Kyle, left Marchwood in February 2016. Alistair Penhaligon, the man=
aging member, retired in 2020. Neither is reachable through Respondent's co=
unsel and I have not attempted direct contact for obvious reasons.<br />
